From 47e3fea31406c82b9f5b3ad367701ced481975ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 01:31:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] citations: stop the published documents pointing a reader at
 files a clone does not contain

README.md and both release documents cite receipt paths like r66-evidence/74-series-check.txt. Those are TRUE statements about where the receipt lives - a lane worktree - and FALSE as paths in a clone. A public README of an attribution-first fork that points at a file the clone does not have is the failure this branch exists to prevent. Each document now carries a note at its head and points at evidence/README.md. The citations are kept: deleting a true fact to make a link stop dangling would be the wrong repair.

evidence/README.md now states that 10-memtypes.txt is NOT byte-identical to the lane receipt - one prose line naming an absolute studio path was placeholder-scrubbed - and points at the unedited original in the fork history. An edited receipt presented as a receipt is the same class of problem as a bare PASS.

The export-branch proposal named git filter-repo as its tool without checking: it is NOT installed on this box (git filter-repo --version returns 'not a git command'). The plan now says so, names the deprecated fallback, and records that no part of that command has been run. docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md was verified tracked, so the merged README section's reference to it resolves.

Also recorded: 5c8d176b7's message says tracked 5727 -> 5161; the true figure is 5164, because three .cmd files with hyphenated stems were missed by that pass and removed in the next one.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - documents only; no code path is touched.
